  "The attack jets (F-61V, F-39E) import the Mk82 weapon file and the fighter jets (F-97 Kestrel, Su-57) the GBU-39 weapon file, each importing the projectile of the same name. The file names are therefore the right way round.",
  "By the L3323 rule the Mk82 file gives 410 to 535 against tanks, 1455 against helicopters; the GBU-39 file gives 300 to 400 and 1080. EA's 1.3.1.0 notes list these two sets under the opposite names, so the notes' two lines are crossed relative to stored data, or the two bombs' values were exchanged after 1.3.1.0. Stored data cannot tell these apart.",
  "On today's stored values the attack jet's bomb is the stronger one."
 ],
